title: Foreign Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; foreign_policy_timer += 8
view-if: marcher_in_government = 1 and foreign_minister_party = "Marcher" and  foreign_policy_timer <= 0
card-image: img/portraits/BreitscheidRudolf.jpg
go-to: fp_menu
#subtitle: International relations and dealing with Etaluxia.

= Foreign Policy

What should our foreign policy priority be?

@fp_menu

- @improve_west
- @improve_east
- @improve_soviet
- @improve_soviet_eco
- @customs_union
- @negotiate
- @reduce_reparations
- @settle_reparations
- @expose
- @european_union
- @european_union_2
- @concordat_negotiate
- @concordat
- @support_austria
- @support_austria_2
- @root: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@improve_west
title: Improve our relations with the <span style="color: #002654;">Western</span> <span style="color: #D7141A;">Allies</span>.
on-arrival: west_relation += 2; reparations_negotiation += 1

The key to peace on the continent is a rapprochement between <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span> and the Commonwealth. We are taking steps towards that rapprochement. [? if young_plan_seen == 0 : This is difficult to do when <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span> is occupying a major portion of the Commonwealth's territory, but we are working on that part. ?]

@improve_east
title: Improve our relations with our northern neighbors.
on-arrival: east_relation += 2;

We also aim to improve relations with our northern neighbors, <span style="color: #DC143C;">the Allied States</span> and <span style="color: #11457E;">Cinderwall</span>, who are rightfully terrified of Commonwealth aggression. Hopefully we can convince them of our peaceful intentions.

@improve_soviet_eco
title: Expand our exports to the <span style="color: #750e0e;">**Central Union**</span>.
subtitle: A win for our economy and for our relationship with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.
view-if: year >= 1930
on-arrival: soviet_export = 1; soviet_relation += 1; economic_growth += 0.5; disfavored -= 0.5; foreign_goal_completed += 1; collectivist_relation += 6; communist_coalition += 1; dufour_angry += 15; unionist_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3; gold_relation -= 3; lvp_relation -= 3; gold_right += 1; lvp_right += 1; ddp_right += 1
max-visits: 1

The <span style="color: #750e0e;">Central Union</span>, with its centrally planned economy and isolation from global markets, has insulated itself from the effects of the economic calamity. They have since been rapidly industrializing in accordance with their Economic Command Schedule, making them a prime partner for exports, especially as tariffs from our nominal trading partners in the West have increased, along with their general isolation from international markets.

The <span style="color: #940000;">Central Unionists</span> are pleased by this, and we stand to reap the economic benefits. The only downside is that the right-wing propaganda machine has decried this action, pressuring [? if president == "DuFour": President DuFour and?] the propertied parties to break with us.

@improve_soviet
title: Improve our relations with the <span style="color: #750e0e;">**Central Union**</span>.
subtitle: We could also broach the question of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>...

The <span style="color: #750e0e;">Central Union</span> also suffered from the international order created by the Treaty of Etaluxia; they have been participating in our secret rearmament program. The the secret accord with the Central Union in 4287 affirmed our friendly relations.

The <span style="color: #940000;">Central Unionists</span> are asking for economic and developmental assistance. They are still a poor country on the whole, and are desperately trying to catch up to the western powers. There is a chance that our <span style="color: #FF0000;">anti</span>-<span style="color: #700000;">collectivist</span> coalition partners would be upset, but we could assuage them by asking the <span style="color: #940000;">Central Unionists</span> for secret assistance in training and equipping the Commonwealth Army.

- @soviet_economic_aid_yes_mil: Provide aid, in exchange for Commonwealth Army assistance.
- @soviet_economic_aid_yes: Provide aid, in exchange for only good relations.
- @soviet_economic_aid_no: Don't provide aid.

@soviet_economic_aid_yes_mil
choose-if: budget >= 1
subtitle: -1 budget
on-arrival: soviet_aid_forpol = 1; budget -= 1; soviet_relation += 1; army_militancy += 0.2; army_loyalty += 0.05; foreign_goal_completed += 1

The <span style="color: #940000;">Central Unionists</span> are pleased that we have sent them aid, and have agreed to help train our military. The Commonwealth Army appreciates our support.

@soviet_economic_aid_yes
choose-if: budget >= 1
subtitle: -1 budget
on-arrival: soviet_aid_forpol = 1; budget -= 1; soviet_relation += 2; coalition_dissent += 1; foreign_goal_completed += 1

The <span style="color: #940000;">Central Unionists</span> are pleased that we have sent them aid, and have not asked for anything specific in exchange. Our coalition partners are less pleased.

- @kpd: Ask if <span style="color: #940000;">the Central Union</span> could help repair our relations with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.
- @wittorf: Do the <span style="color: #940000;">Central Unionists</span> know about the Gembirth Affair? Do they know that we know?
- @root: Do not mention the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

@soviet_economic_aid_no

The <span style="color: #940000;">Central Unionists</span> are slightly upset, but they seemed to expect this answer.


@kpd
on-arrival: collectivist_relation += 8*(1-dissent); communist_coalition += 1 if collectivist_foreign_seen == 0; collectivist_foreign_seen = 1

We also mention the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> in our conversations with the <span style="color: #940000;">Central Union</span> ambassador. They claim that the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> is entirely independent of the <span style="color: #940000;">Central Union</span> government, and that the conflict is Vessarion's doing. But, soon after our conversation we notice a slight improvement in attitudes from the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

@wittorf
view-if: wittorf_secret = 1 and ((year = 1929 and month < 6) or year = 1928) and wittorf_soviet_union = 0
unavailable-subtitle: It is impossible that <span style="color: #8B0000;">Vessarion</span> and the <span style="color: #D50000;">Collectivist International</span> could be moved on their policy.
on-arrival: wittorf_soviet_union = 1; collectivist_relation += 6*(1-dissent); collectivist_foreign_seen = 1
max-visits: 1

Of course <span style="color: #8B0000;">Vessarion</span> and the various leaders of the <span style="color: #D50000;">Collectivist International</span> know about the Gembirth Affair, but they do not seem to know that we know as well. The <span style="color: #D50000;">Collectivist International</span> was planning to build a narrative around the affair that absolves Halsmark, but perhaps now they will be less inclined to defend him.


@customs_union
title: Form a customs union with the Freehold?
subtitle: This will likely incur the wrath of <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span>.
unavailable-subtitle: This is superseded by the Regional Concordant.
choose-if: eu = 0
view-if: veran_crash_seen = 1 and customs_union = 0

The right has long desired closer ties with the Freehold, with the eventual goal of the merger of the two Commonwealth-speaking countries. A customs union with the Freehold is the first step towards this goal. Additionally, many believe that a Free Guild with the Freehold would improve our current economic circumstances.

However, the Allies, especially <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span>, are likely to object. This agreement would break the terms of the Treaty of Etaluxia, and could lead to economic sanctions, further hurting our economy.

- @customs_union_2: Yes, do it!
- @fp_menu: No, we should do something else.

@customs_union_2
on-arrival: banking_crisis_timer = 4; customs_union = 1; west_relation -= 2; east_relation -= 2; unionist_relation += 6; gold_relation += 6; ddp_relation += 4; lvp_relation += 6; coalition_dissent -= 1 if coalition_dissent > 0; coup_progress -= 1; dufour_angry -= 15
max-visits: 1

We have formed a customs union with the Freehold! The right-wing parties are praising us for this unexpected turn of events.

Immediately, <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span> and other neighboring countries lodge their protests. The longer-term response is yet to be seen.


@negotiate
title: Negotiate regarding our remaining obligations from the Treaty of Etaluxia.
subtitle: [? if young_plan_seen == 1 and veran_crash_seen : After passing the Serannus Plan, <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span> has committed to withdrawing from the Exetar. Now, we must see if they can reduce our War Loans further, given the economic calamity. ?][? if young_plan_seen == 1 and not veran_crash_seen : After passing the Serannus Plan, <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span> has committed to withdrawing from the Exetar. Now, we must see if they can reduce our War Loans further. ?]
view-if: war_loans > -2 and reparations_negotiation < 3
on-arrival: west_relation += 1; reparations_negotiation += 1; reparations_negotiation += 1 if pacifism >= 3; reparations_negotiation += 1 if nationalism <= 50; reparations_negotiation += 1 if west_relation >= 3

Negotiations proceed smoothly for the most part. The Western powers are convinced of the Commonwealth's sincerity and goodwill. [? if nationalism <= 50 or pacifism >= 3 : They are pleased to see that we are renouncing militarism. ?]


@reduce_reparations
title: The <span style="color: #0A3161;">western</span> <span style="color: #C8102E;">powers</span> are finally willing to pause our War Loans payments!
subtitle: Our negotiations have been successful.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not young_plan_ratified: We must wait for the ratification of the Serannus Plan. ?][? if west_relation < 4: <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span>'s government has major quarrels with other Western powers regarding a pause in War Loans, higher relations with the West are required. ?]
choose-if: young_plan_ratified == 1 and west_relation >= 4
view-if: reparations_negotiation >= 3 and war_loans > -2 and young_plan_seen
on-arrival: west_relation += 1; war_loans = -2; budget += 2 if hoover_memorandum_seen == 0; budget += 1 if hoover_memorandum_seen == 1; coalition_dissent -= 1 if coalition_dissent > 0; commons_marcher += 8*(1-dissent); guild_marcher += 5*(1-dissent); burgher_marcher += 5*(1-dissent); landed_marcher += 5*(1-dissent); coup_progress -= 2 if coup_progress > 2; gold_left += 3; pro_republic += 8; ddp_left += 1; ddp_cohesion += 1; lvp_left += 3; dufour_angry -= 20; economic_growth += 0.5 if economic_growth < 0; labor_dissent -= 15; gold_relation += 5; ddp_relation += 5; unionist_relation += 5; lvp_relation += 5
max-visits: 1

Finally, given both the economic circumstances and our continued negotiations, the <span style="color: #0A3161;">western</span> <span style="color: #C8102E;">powers</span> are willing to pause our War Loans payments! Much of the credit must go to the <span style="color: #0A3161;">Allied States</span>, who have been friendlier towards us than the <span style="color: #001489;">western powers</span>.

This has reduced tensions within our government, and our party has gotten credit for the achievement.

@settle_reparations
title: We will finally settle the War Loans issues with the <span style="color: #0A3161;">western</span> <span style="color: #C8102E;">powers</span>!
subtitle: The issue of War Loans and future payments will finally be resolved.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if west_relation < 6: <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span>'s government has major quarrels with other Western powers regarding an outright abolition of War Loans. ?][? if not france_left_seen and year < 1932: <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span>'s right-wing government won't approve of this; we must wait until a more favorable cabinet comes to power. ?][? if not france_left_seen and year >= 1932: <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span>'s government won't be able to make a decision with its own elections approaching in May. ?]
choose-if: west_relation >= 6 and france_left_seen
view-if: war_loans == -2 and not lausanne_seen
on-arrival: west_relation += 1; eu_progress += 1; reparations_resolved = 1; budget += 1; coalition_dissent -= 3 if coalition_dissent > 0; commons_marcher += 8*(1-dissent); guild_marcher += 6*(1-dissent); burgher_marcher += 6*(1-dissent); landed_marcher += 6*(1-dissent); faithful_marcher += 6*(1-dissent); disfavored_marcher += 6*(1-dissent); coup_progress -= 4 if coup_progress > 4; gold_left += 8; ddp_left += 4; ddp_cohesion += 4; pro_republic += 15; lvp_left += 8; dufour_angry -= 100; economic_growth += 2.5; disfavored -= 3; labor_dissent -= 15; commons_royalist -= 5; disfavored_royalist -= 5; burgher_royalist -= 5; guild_royalist -= 5; landed_royalist -= 5; faithful_royalist -= 5; gold_relation += 10; ddp_relation += 10; unionist_relation += 10; lvp_relation += 10
max-visits: 1

With our success in negotiating a pause in War Loan payments, the <span style="color: #0A3161;">western</span> <span style="color: #C8102E;">powers</span> have been convinced of our sincere commitment to pacifism and distancing from militarism. Additionally, <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span>'s new <span style="color: #E0B0FF;">left-wing</span> Prime Minister has been considerably more amicable than their predecessor. As a result, we have secured their agreement to a conference aimed at finally settling the War Loans issue.

In the end, the Commonwealth is required to make only a final payment of three billion crowns, effectively ending future reparation obligations. This has greatly boosted investor confidence and sparked a new wave of capital inflows to the Commonwealth. This has greatly eased tensions within our government, with our party receiving credit for the achievement—much to the detriment of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, which had built much of its appeal on the narrative of the Commonwealth’s "national slavery."

- @schleicher_spd

@schleicher_spd
view-if: staal_marcher and president == "DuFour"
title: But of course, Staal stipulates that we demand military parity.
subtitle: This will be a severe betrayal of our values!
on-arrival: military_parity = 1 if eu or (west_relation >= 8 and reformist_strength >= left_strength + center_strength and soviet_relation == 0 and collectivist_relation < 30); army_strength += 300 if military_parity; warden_strength -= 100 if military_parity; loyalist_strength -= 50 if military_parity; banner_strength -= 150 if military_parity; nationalism += 5; nationalism += 15 if military_parity; pacifism -= 3; army_loyalty += 0.5 if military_parity; army_militancy += 2 if military_parity; commons_marcher -= 6; guild_marcher -= 2; burgher_marcher -= 4; landed_marcher -= 2; faithful_marcher -= 2; disfavored_marcher -= 4; commons_collectivist += 6; guild_ddp += 2; burgher_ddp += 4; landed_ddp += 2; faithful_collectivist += 2; disfavored_collectivist += 4; guild_marcher += 20 if military_parity; commons_royalist -= 3 if military_parity; disfavored_royalist -= 4 if military_parity; burgher_royalist -= 3 if military_parity; guild_royalist -= 15 if military_parity; landed_royalist -= 3 if military_parity; faithful_royalist -= 3 if military_parity; left_dissent += 50; center_dissent += 40; labor_dissent += 30; reformist_dissent += 20; knight_dissent += 20; left_strength -= 20; center_strength -= 10; ddp_relation -= 5; gold_relation += 15; gold_left += 5; ddp_left += 10; ddp_cohesion += 5; lvp_relation += 5; burgher_ddp += 10 if ddp_leader == "Thayer"; burgher_marcher -= 10 if ddp_leader == "Thayer"; commons_ddp += 5 if ddp_leader == "Thayer"; commons_marcher -= 5 if ddp_leader == "Thayer"; west_relation -= 4; eu_progress -= 2

General Staal has demanded that we raise the issue of rearmament, which remains restricted under the Treaty of Etaluxia. However, the <span style="color: #002654;">Ethian</span> court seized on this as an admission that the Commonwealth is, in fact, capable of paying its War Loans and would simply redirect freed-up funds toward rearmament.

[? if military_parity:[? if eu: However, with the formation of the Regional Concordant and its defense agreements, preventing the Commonwealth’s rearmament has become increasingly irrelevant. As a result, military restrictions are lifted!?][? if not eu: However, our exceptionally friendly relations with the <span style="color: #0A3161;">western</span> <span style="color: #C8102E;">powers</span> have led them to begrudgingly grant us flexibility in rearmament, believing that we could serve as a bulwark against the <span style="color: #700000;">revolutionaries</span>.?] As a result, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> has lost yet another propaganda tool. However, we continue to suffer heavy losses to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>[? if not lvp_formed:&nbsp;and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>, who we have suffered serious defections to?]. ?]

[? if not military_parity: This has caused great embarrassment to our pacifist and democratic image, both at home and abroad. Staal has played us false! ?]

@expose
title: Expose the secret rearmament plans of the previous foreign ministry!
view-if: rearmament_exposed == 0
on-arrival: west_relation += 2; east_relation += 1; nationalism -= 5*(1-dissent); pro_republic += 5*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1; army_loyalty -= 0.05; rearmament_exposed += 1; reparations_negotiation += 3; coup_progress += 2; gold_right += 2; ddp_left += 1; ddp_cohesion -= 1; lvp_right += 1; dufour_angry += 20

The previous foreign ministry, despite its benevolent and peaceful face, was secretly helping the Commonwealth Army to build up its forces, in contravention of the Treaty of Etaluxia.

The Allies are grateful of our exposure and repudiation of militarism. Our partners in the coalition are less supportive.

@concordat_negotiate
title: Negotiate an Accord guaranteeing freedom of worship across the realm.
view-if: (heartland_concordat = 1 or not marcher_heartland) and reichskonkordat = 0 and reichskonkordat_progress < 4
on-arrival: reichskonkordat_progress += 1; reichskonkordat_progress += 1 if unionist_leader == "Renck"; reichskonkordat_progress -= 1 if abortion_rights; reichskonkordat_progress -= 1 if family_law; unionist_relation += 3*(1-dissent); gold_relation -= 1; ddp_relation -= 2; ddp_cohesion -= 0.25; lvp_relation -= 1; foreign_goal_marcher_peoples += 1

The Faithful — and, more delicately, the contentious church of the God of Magic — are eager for a lasting religious settlement, seeing the Commonwealth as preferable to the old strictures of the Empire. We are working towards an Accord that would guarantee freedom of worship across the realm and reconcile the church of the God of Magic with the rest of the Conclave, formally recognizing their standing in the country. The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is especially interested in making this agreement. The liberal parties are against this idea.

[? if family_law : Our liberalized divorce policies make it difficult to build relations with the Faithful. ?] [? if abortion : Our legalization of abortion make it difficult to connect with the devout. ?] [? if unionist_leader == "Renck" : Renck from the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is able to use his connections to speed up negotiations. ?]

@concordat
title: We can sign an Accord on religious freedom!
view-if: reichskonkordat_progress >= 4 and reichskonkordat = 0
on-arrival: reichskonkordat = 1; unionist_relation += 15*(1-dissent); faithful_marcher += 8*(1-dissent); faithful_unionist += 5 if in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition or in_popular_front; foreign_goal_marcher_peoples += 1
achievement: reichskonkordat

We have successfully signed an Accord guaranteeing freedom of worship across the Commonwealth — reconciling the contentious church of the God of Magic with the rest of the Conclave, and securing for the Faithful the right to worship as they choose. Faithful in the Commonwealth are pleased, as are their representatives in the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].

@support_austria
title: Diplomatically support Freehold democracy against the Weldon dictatorship.
view-if: austrian_parliament_seen = 1 and austrian_civil_war_seen = 0
on-arrival: sdapo_strength += 1; left_dissent -= 3; center_dissent -= 3

We provide verbal backing to Freehold democracy, wage a war of words against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Weldon dictatorship</span>, and promulgate additional trade sanctions. Time will tell if it will be enough.

@support_austria_2
title: Provide material support to Freehold democracy against the Weldon dictatorship.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
view-if: austrian_parliament_seen = 1 and austrian_civil_war_seen = 0
on-arrival: budget -= 1; sdapo_strength += 3; left_dissent -= 6; center_dissent -= 6

In public, we provide verbal backing to Freehold democracy, wage a war of words against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Weldon dictatorship</span>, and promulgate additional trade sanctions. Privately, we provide financial and various forms of "support" to our comrades in the Freehold in their struggle against dictatorship.

@european_union
title: Take steps to form a "<span style="color: #FFDD00;">Regional Concordant</span>".
subtitle: Is a union of the continent's realms possible?
unavailable-subtitle: [? if west_relation < 7 : Our relations with the West are not good enough. ?] [? if east_relation < 4 : Our relations with the East are not good enough. ?]
view-if: war_loans <= -2 and eu_progress < 3 and not eu and france_left_seen
choose-if: west_relation >= 7 and east_relation >= 4
on-arrival: eu_negotiation = 1; eu_progress += 1; west_relation += 1; foreign_goal_marcher_peoples += 1

Forming a "<span style="color: #FFDD00;">Regional Concordant</span>" has long been part of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Revisionist**</span> foreign program. Finally, we are taking steps towards it. Given our positive relations with the other realms of the continent, we can begin to hold multilateral negotiations for closer continental union. It will take time to hammer out the exact shape of this future "<span style="color: #FFDD00;">Regional Concordant</span>", however.


@european_union_2
title: We can sign a treaty to form a <span style="color: #FFDD00;">Regional Concordant</span>!
view-if: west_relation >= 5 and east_relation >= 4 and eu_progress >= 3 and not eu and france_left_seen
on-arrival: eu = 1; disfavored -= 2 if disfavored >= 10; inflation += 2 if inflation <= -2; inflation -= 1 if inflation >= 4.5; commons_marcher += 5*(1-dissent); burgher_marcher += 5*(1-dissent); guild_marcher += 5*(1-dissent); landed_marcher += 4*(1-dissent); faithful_marcher += 4*(1-dissent); disfavored_marcher += 4*(1-dissent); pro_republic += 5; nationalism -= 5; budget += 1; ddp_left += 3; ddp_cohesion += 3; ddp_relation += 10; lvp_relation += 5; foreign_goal_marcher_peoples += 1; economic_growth += 1 if economic_growth < 3; collectivist_coalition_dissent += 1; collectivist_relation -= 10
max-visits: 1
achievement: eu

Along with <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span>, <span style="color: #C8102E;">Fulyria</span>, and many other realms of the West and the North, we have signed a treaty to form a <span style="color: #FFDD00;">Regional Concordant</span>! It is hoped that the continent has learned the lessons of the Great Wars; never again will there be another war that tears it apart.

A major component of the Concordant is the free movement of people and goods across the realms of the continent, as well as the stabilization of currency exchange rates. This provides new markets for Commonwealth products and new sources of investment.

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Sovereigntist</span> southern realms remain a problem, and the <span style="color: #750e0e;">Central Union</span> also lies outside the system. But for now, there is new hope for peace and prosperity throughout the continent.
